schema: signal
object:
  title: "Format determines outcome more than topic — and open house is the best burnout defense"
  type: signal
  signal_type: track
  affected_layer: layer-7-tracks
  interpretation: >-
    Two reusable patterns worth carrying into any future local-node-onboarding
    track: (1) the same topic run through a different container produces a
    different outcome (a lecture on governance produces passive listeners;
    a fishbowl discussion on the same topic produces engaged co-thinkers), so
    format should be chosen deliberately, not defaulted to; (2) among all
    the formats in this guide, the recurring open house is named explicitly
    as the single best burnout defense for a node host (low cost, high
    consistency, keeps the node visible between bigger events) — worth
    surfacing as a starter recommendation whenever a node onboarding track
    is built.
  proposed_intervention: cite
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/types-of-gatherings.md
    transformation: inferred
    authorship: ai-assisted
  source_lineage: types-of-gatherings.md
